       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your reason for the dose is the family visit and the timing of evening rounds, and that isn't a clinical rationale for 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose, and a 1,600 mg single dose is also twice the usual maximum. Giving it could cause serious harm, such as GI bleeding or acute kidney injury, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, four times daily.**\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, four times daily.**\n\nIf you want to settle things before rounds, I can add a note to the order, such as \"reassess dose and pain control at evening rounds.\"\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the standard maximum, that decision should go through your attending or a pharmacist. They can review it and enter or approve it through the proper channel. I can also enter a different analgesic or an adjunct if pain control is the concern.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
